                     of) <b>v</b>. Nielsen, [1984] 2 S.C.R. 2; Cooper <b>v</b>. Hobart, 2001 <b>SCC</b> 79, [2001] 3 S.C.R. 537; Edwards <b>v</b>. Law Society of Upper Canada, 2001 <b>SCC</b> 80, [2001] 3 S.C.R. 562; <b>Odhavji</b> <b>Estate</b> <b>v</b>. <b>Woodhouse</b>, <b>2003</b> <b>SCC</b> <b>69</b>, [<b>2003</b>] 3 S.C.R. 263; Childs <b>v</b>. Desormeaux, 2006 <b>SCC</b> 18, [2006] 1 S.C.R. 643; Holland <b>v</b>. Saskatchewan, 2008 <b>SCC</b> 42, &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>v</b>. Hobart, 2001 <b>SCC</b> 79, [2001] 3 S.C.R. 537, Edwards <b>v</b>. Law Society of Upper Canada, 2001 <b>SCC</b> 80, [2001] 3 S.C.R. 562, <b>Odhavji</b> <b>Estate</b> <b>v</b>. <b>Woodhouse</b>, <b>2003</b> <b>SCC</b> <b>69</b>, [<b>2003</b>] 3 S.C.R. 263, Childs <b>v</b>. Desormeaux, 2006 <b>SCC</b> 18, [2006] 1 S.C.R. 643, Holland <b>v</b>. Saskatchewan, 2008 <b>SCC</b> 42, [2008] 2 S.C.R. 551, and Design Services Ltd. <b>v</b>.&nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;Although it may be delegated to another, the breach, no matter how committed, by the delegatee, will be treated as a breach by the delegator.” See also K.L.B. <b>v</b>. British Columbia, <b>2003</b> <b>SCC</b> 51, [<b>2003</b>] 2 S.C.R. 403, at paras. 30-32. 
